

1) CHECK NETWORK ON BOTH HOST1 AND HOST2
----------------------------------------
ip -br addr
ip route
ls /etc/netplan/

2) EDIT NETPLAN (ONLY AFTER CONFIRMING SUBNET AND INTERFACE)
-----------------------------------------------------------
sudo nano /etc/netplan/YOUR-FILE.yaml

Example Host1 configuration (replace ens33 and subnet if different):
network:
  version: 2
  ethernets:
    ens33:
      dhcp4: false
      addresses:
        - 192.168.56.101/24

Example Host2 configuration: use 192.168.56.102/24 instead.

Save Nano: Ctrl+O, Enter, Ctrl+X.

Apply on both hosts (replace filename as needed):
sudo chmod 600 /etc/netplan/YOUR-FILE.yaml
sudo netplan generate
sudo netplan try
sudo netplan apply
ip -br addr
ip route

